      "title": "NCLT completely hijacked by Ministry of Corporate Affairs: Supreme Court",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/industry/news/nclt-completely-hijacked-by-ministry-of-corporate-affairs-supreme-court-126102900696_1.html",
      "description": "In a stinging remark, the Supreme Court on Thursday orally remarked that the Ministry of Corporate Affairs has completely hijacked the National Company Law Tribunal and its appellate body, NCLAT.\nWhile calling for autonomy for the NCLT and NCLAT presidents over appointments, a bench comprising Chief Justice Surya Kant, Justices Joymalya Bagchi and V Mohana suggested deputation as an interim measure and phased regular recruitment through UPSC or SSC.\n\"I know how contractors play their hands. They don't care about judicial/technical members. Complete autonomy must be with presidents. They can take UPSC/SSC. The tribunal has been completely hijacked by the Ministry of Corporate Affairs. That is impinging on the autonomy of the institution. That's the problem. The ministry wants to have complete grip; that's most unfortunate,\" CJI orally remarked.\nThe observations were made while hearing a petition filed by contractual employees working in the NCLT and National Company Law Appellate ...",
